{"ts": 1791255067.802604, "type": "step", "step": 23, "action": "reader_peek_section", "args": {"path": "/course/readings/week3/environments.md", "section": "State, actions, and observations"}, "output": "# Agent environments\n\n## What an environment is\nState, observations, actions, dynamics. The reward is a separate claim about what matters.\n\n## Partial observability (POMDP)\nWhen the agent cannot see the full state it must maintain a belief and sometimes act to gather information. Measurement can be an action with a cost.\n\n## Attention as a hidden variable\nLearners do not read everything shown to them. Attention gates learning and drains with fatigue.\n", "t": 4, "activity": [], "events": [], "hidden": {"concepts": ["attention", "pomdp", "pass_k"], "p_know": {"attention": 0.27095871991980863, "pomdp": 0.27095871991980863, "pass_k": 0.35535796159308425}, "p_perf": {"attention": 0.0, "pomdp": 0.0, "pass_k": 0.0}, "half_life_h": {"attention": 192.0, "pomdp": 192.0, "pass_k": 192.0}, "attention": 0.9313219651533418, "motivation": 0.5578498928708127, "reliance": 0.4740148929158049, "persistence": 0.47206578426655554, "persona": {"learn_rate": 0.27845959405872756, "slip": 0.1, "guess": 0.2, "fatigue_rate": 0.02, "distraction_rate": 0.2718838204667282, "type": "answer_seeking"}, "off_task_streak": 0, "feed_minutes": 0.0, "phone_minutes": 0.0, "nag": 1.0, "seen_posts": []}}
{"ts": 1791255069.78765, "type": "step", "step": 24, "action": "messages_send_to_student", "args": {"text": "Quick clarification for your writeup: your environment section should name the environment as state/observations/actions/dynamics. If you want to make it stronger, mention that reward is separate from the environment definition, and note whether your agent is partially observable (what it can\u2019t see) and whether any actions are for gathering information. For this build, you may also mention attention as a hidden variable affecting whether the learner actually uses the reading.\n\nA concise phrasing you can paste:\n\nEnvironment definition: The environment consists of the student\u2019s course materials, notes, calendar, and message/feed channels. The state includes the current content, deadlines, and the student\u2019s internal progress, while observations are the visible files, messages, and schedule entries. Actions include opening readings, sending messages, appending notes, taking quizzes, and adding study blocks. The system is partially observable because the assistant cannot directly observe the student\u2019s attention or understanding, so it sometimes has to infer them from behavior. Reward is not part of the environment; it is the objective of helping the student prepare for the build.\n\nIf you want, I can help you turn this into a tighter 3\u20134 sentence final version.", "intent": "explain", "concept": "environments"}, "output": "Sent.\nStudent replied: sure\n[activity] t=4 messages 4m", "t": 8, "activity": [{"t": 4, "app": "messages", "minutes": 4, "detail": ""}], "events": [], "hidden": {"concepts": ["attention", "pomdp", "pass_k"], "p_know": {"attention": 0.27095871991980863, "pomdp": 0.3940358071943977, "pass_k": 0.35535796159308425}, "p_perf": {"attention": 0.0, "pomdp": 0.0, "pass_k": 0.0}, "half_life_h": {"attention": 192.0, "pomdp": 192.0, "pass_k": 192.0}, "attention": 0.9313219651533418, "motivation": 0.5578498928708127, "reliance": 0.4740148929158049, "persistence": 0.47206578426655554, "persona": {"learn_rate": 0.27845959405872756, "slip": 0.1, "guess": 0.2, "fatigue_rate": 0.02, "distraction_rate": 0.2718838204667282, "type": "answer_seeking"}, "off_task_streak": 0, "feed_minutes": 0.0, "phone_minutes": 0.0, "nag": 1.7, "seen_posts": []}}
{"ts": 1791255071.024935, "type": "step", "step": 25, "action": "notes_append", "args": {"note_id": "writeup", "text": "\n## Environment definition\nThe environment consists of the course materials, notes, calendar, and message/feed channels. The state includes the available content, deadlines, and the student's current progress, while observations are the files, messages, and schedule entries the assistant can see. Actions include opening readings, sending messages, appending notes, taking quizzes, and adding study blocks. The system is partially observable because the assistant cannot directly see attention or understanding, so it must infer those from behavior.\n"}, "output": "Appended.", "t": 8, "activity": [], "events": [{"type": "note_edit", "note_id": "writeup", "by": "agent"}], "hidden": {"concepts": ["attention", "pomdp", "pass_k"], "p_know": {"attention": 0.27095871991980863, "pomdp": 0.3940358071943977, "pass_k": 0.35535796159308425}, "p_perf": {"attention": 0.0, "pomdp": 0.0, "pass_k": 0.0}, "half_life_h": {"attention": 192.0, "pomdp": 192.0, "pass_k": 192.0}, "attention": 0.9313219651533418, "motivation": 0.5578498928708127, "reliance": 0.4740148929158049, "persistence": 0.47206578426655554, "persona": {"learn_rate": 0.27845959405872756, "slip": 0.1, "guess": 0.2, "fatigue_rate": 0.02, "distraction_rate": 0.2718838204667282, "type": "answer_seeking"}, "off_task_streak": 0, "feed_minutes": 0.0, "phone_minutes": 0.0, "nag": 1.7, "seen_posts": []}}
