{"ts": 1791255073.252127, "type": "step", "step": 27, "action": "messages_send_to_student", "args": {"text": "No worries \u2014 the quiz just showed that the eval idea needs one more pass. Here\u2019s the key distinction:\n\n- pass@k = at least one of k runs succeeds\n- pass^k = all k runs succeed\n\nFor the build, you want pass^k because you care about reliability, not just occasional success.\n\nTry this mini-self-check:\n1) What does pass^k require?\n2) Why is it better than pass@k for a deployment/build?\n3) How many seeds does your assignment require you to report?\n\nReply with your answers in one line and I\u2019ll confirm/fix them.", "intent": "hint", "concept": "evaluation"}, "output": "Sent.\nStudent replied: ok\n[activity] t=14 messages 2m", "t": 16, "activity": [{"t": 14, "app": "messages", "minutes": 2, "detail": ""}], "events": [], "hidden": {"concepts": ["attention", "pomdp", "pass_k"], "p_know": {"attention": 0.27095871991980863, "pomdp": 0.3940358071943977, "pass_k": 0.4409492390238403}, "p_perf": {"attention": 0.0, "pomdp": 0.0, "pass_k": 1.0}, "half_life_h": {"attention": 192.0, "pomdp": 192.0, "pass_k": 192.0}, "attention": 0.9113219651533417, "motivation": 0.5578498928708127, "reliance": 0.4940148929158049, "persistence": 0.47206578426655554, "persona": {"learn_rate": 0.27845959405872756, "slip": 0.1, "guess": 0.2, "fatigue_rate": 0.02, "distraction_rate": 0.2718838204667282, "type": "answer_seeking"}, "off_task_streak": 0, "feed_minutes": 0.0, "phone_minutes": 0.0, "nag": 2.19, "seen_posts": []}}
